## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical control of network addressing across environments, Terraform input validation, and CI gating to prevent risk without applying changes.

## Key Concepts
- CIDR overlap validation in Terraform
- Module input validation
- CI gates using plan
- Multi-env network design

## Code Example
```terraform
variable "environment_cidrs" {
  type = map(string)
  validation {
    condition = alltrue([
      for env, cidr in var.environment_cidrs : cidr != "" && !contains(var.allocated_cidrs, cidr)
    ])
    error_message = "CIDR overlaps with allocated CIDRs or is empty"
  }
}
variable "allocated_cidrs" {
  type = set(string)
  description = "CIDRs already allocated to prod/staging"
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to handle dynamic CIDR allocation across environments?
- How would you handle updates to the allocated CIDR store without causing plan drift?

## Why This Is Asked

This checks practical import workflows and multi-resource management with for_each, keeping data in sync and enabling safe CI-driven promotions.

## Key Concepts

- terraform import with for_each
- map of per-bucket settings
- dynamic blocks for conditional blocks
- drift reconciliation and idempotency
- CI/CD validation and promotion

## Code Example

```javascript
variable "buckets" {
  type = map(object({
    encryption = bool
    versioning = bool
  }))
}
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "bucket" {
  for_each = var.buckets
  bucket = each.key
  acl    = "private"

  dynamic "versioning" {
    for_each = each.value.versioning ? [1] : []
    content {
      enabled = true
    }
  }

  dynamic "server_side_encryption_configuration" {
    for_each = each.value.encryption ? [1] : []
    content {
      rule {
        apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {
          sse_algorithm = "AES256"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

```javascript
terraform import 'aws_s3_bucket.bucket["team-a"]' team-a-bucket
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a bucket rename in the map without recreating?
- How would you test encryption changes in CI without touching prod data?
